{"id":"mahabharata-2-003","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":3,"title":"तृतीयोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 3 · Maya builds the hall","summary":{"en":"Maya goes to Lake Bindusaras in the north and brings back the treasures of the demon king Vrishaparvan, a mighty mace for Bhima and the conch Devadatta for Arjuna. In fourteen months he builds a hall of dazzling jewels, crystal pools and golden trees, guarded by eight thousand Rakshasas, and presents it to Yudhishthira.","kn":"ಮಯನು ಉತ್ತರದ ಬಿಂದುಸರಸ್ಸಿಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ ದೈತ್ಯರಾಜ ವೃಷಪರ್ವನ ಸಂಪತ್ತನ್ನೂ, ಭೀಮನಿಗೆ ಮಹಾಗದೆಯನ್ನೂ, ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ದೇವದತ್ತ ಶಂಖವನ್ನೂ ತರುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹದಿನಾಲ್ಕು ತಿಂಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಬೆರಗುಗೊಳಿಸುವ ರತ್ನಗಳ, ಸ್ಫಟಿಕ ಕೊಳಗಳ, ಚಿನ್ನದ ಮರಗಳ, ಎಂಟು ಸಾವಿರ ರಾಕ್ಷಸರು ಕಾಯುವ ಸಭೆ ಕಟ್ಟಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಅರ್ಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"मय उत्तर में बिन्दुसर सरोवर जाकर दैत्यराज वृषपर्वा का खज़ाना, भीम के लिए एक विशाल गदा और अर्जुन के लिए देवदत्त शंख लाता है। चौदह महीनों में वह चमचमाते रत्नों, स्फटिक के सरोवरों और स्वर्ण-वृक्षों वाली, आठ हज़ार राक्षसों से रक्षित सभा बनाकर युधिष्ठिर को सौंपता है।","te":"మయుడు ఉత్తరాన బిందుసరస్సుకు వెళ్లి దైత్యరాజు వృషపర్వుని సంపదను, భీమునికి మహాగదను, అర్జునునికి దేవదత్త శంఖాన్ని తెస్తాడు. పద్నాలుగు నెలలలో మిరుమిట్లు గొలిపే రత్నాలు, స్ఫటిక సరస్సులు, బంగారు చెట్లతో, ఎనిమిదివేల రాక్షసులు కాపలా కాసే సభను నిర్మించి యుధిష్ఠిరునికి సమర్పిస్తాడు.","ta":"மயன் வடக்கிலுள்ள பிந்துஸரஸுக்குச் சென்று அசுர மன்னன் வ்ருஷபர்வனின் செல்வத்தையும், பீமனுக்குப் பெரிய கதையையும், அர்ஜுனனுக்குத் தேவதத்த சங்கையும் கொண்டு வருகிறான். பதினான்கு மாதங்களில் ஒளிரும் ரத்தினங்கள், பளிங்குக் குளங்கள், பொன் மரங்கள் கொண்ட, எண்ணாயிரம் அரக்கர்கள் காக்கும் ஸபையைக் கட்டி யுதிஷ்டிரருக்கு அளிக்கிறான்.","ml":"വടക്ക് ബിന്ദുസരസ്സിൽ പോയി മയൻ, രാക്ഷസരാജാവായ വൃഷപർവ്വാവിന്റെ നിധികൾ കൊണ്ടുവരുന്നു: ഭീമന് ശക്തമായ ഗദയും അർജുനന് ദേവദത്തം എന്ന ശംഖും. പതിന്നാലു മാസം കൊണ്ട് രത്നങ്ങൾകൊണ്ടുള്ള തിളങ്ങുന്ന ഒരു മണ്ഡപം, സ്ഫടികക്കുളങ്ങൾ, സ്വർണമരങ്ങൾ എന്നിവയോടെ അദ്ദേഹം പണിയുന്നു; എണ്ണായിരം രാക്ഷസന്മാർ കാക്കുന്ന അത് യുധിഷ്ഠിരന് സമർപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.3; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"सभापर्व","titleEn":"Sabha Parva (The assembly hall)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथाब्रवीन्मयः पार्थमर्जुनं जयतां वरम् ।\nआपृच्छे त्वां गमिष्यामि क्षिप्रमेष्यामि चाप्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Maya said to Arjuna, the best of victors, \"I take my leave of you; I will go and come back soon."}},{"n":2,"text":"उत्तरेण तु कैलासं मैनाकं पर्वतं प्रति ।\nयक्ष्यमाणेषु सर्वेषु दानवेषु तदा मया ।\nकृतं मणिमयं भाण्डं रम्यं बिन्दुसरः प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"To the north of Kailasa, near the mountain Mainaka, when all the Danavas were about to hold a sacrifice, I made a lovely jeweled treasure near Lake Bindu."}},{"n":3,"text":"सभायां सत्यसंधस्य यदासीद्वृषपर्वणः ।\nआगमिष्यामि तद्गृह्य यदि तिष्ठति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It was in the hall of the truthful Vrishaparvan; I will fetch it, Bharata, if it is still there."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततः सभां करिष्यामि पाण्डवाय यशस्विने ।\nमनःप्रह्लादिनीं चित्रां सर्वरत्नविभूषिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I will build a hall for the renowned Pandava, wonderful, delighting the mind and adorned with every gem."}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्ति बिन्दुसरस्येव गदा श्रेष्ठा कुरूद्वह ।\nनिहिता यौवनाश्वेन राज्ञा हत्वा रणे रिपून् ।\nसुवर्णबिन्दुभिश्चित्रा गुर्वी भारसहा दृढा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is also, at Bindu lake, a superb mace, O Kuru chief, laid down by King Yuvanashva after he killed his enemies in battle; it is heavy and strong, able to bear great weight, studded with golden dots."}},{"n":6,"text":"सा वै शतसहस्रस्य संमिता सर्वघातिनी ।\nअनुरूपा च भीमस्य गाण्डीवं भवतो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It is worth a hundred thousand ordinary maces and kills everything it strikes; it suits Bhima as Gandiva suits you."}},{"n":7,"text":"वारुणश्च महाशङ्खो देवदत्तः सुघोषवान् ।\nसर्वमेतत्प्रदास्यामि भवते नात्र संशयः ।\nइत्युक्त्वा सोऽसुरः पार्थं प्रागुदीचीमगाद्दिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is also Varuna's great conch Devadatta, loud-sounding. I will give all this to you, no doubt.\" Having said this, the Asura went off toward the northeast."}},{"n":8,"text":"उत्तरेण तु कैलासं मैनाकं पर्वतं प्रति ।\nहिरण्यशृङ्गो भगवान्महामणिमयो गिरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"North of Kailasa, near the mountain Mainaka, stands the great jeweled mountain Hiranyashringa."}},{"n":9,"text":"रम्यं बिन्दुसरो नाम यत्र राजा भगीरथः ।\nदृष्ट्वा भागीरथीं गङ्गामुवास बहुलाः समाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There lies the lovely lake Bindu, where King Bhagiratha lived for many years after seeing the Ganga, the Bhagirathi."}},{"n":10,"text":"यत्रेष्ट्वा सर्वभूतानामीश्वरेण महात्मना ।\nआहृताः क्रतवो मुख्याः शतं भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, O best of Bharatas, the great lord of all beings performed a hundred principal sacrifices."}},{"n":11,"text":"यत्र यूपा मणिमयाश्चित्याश्चापि हिरण्मयाः ।\nशोभार्थं विहितास्तत्र न तु दृष्टान्ततः कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the sacrificial posts were of jewels and the altars of gold, set up only for beauty and not as the ritual demands."}},{"n":12,"text":"यत्रेष्ट्वा स गतः सिद्धिं सहस्राक्षः शचीपतिः ।\nयत्र भूतपतिः सृष्ट्वा सर्वलोकान्सनातनः ।\nउपास्यते तिग्मतेजा वृतो भूतैः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Indra of the thousand eyes, husband of Shachi, performed a sacrifice and attained perfection; and there the lord of beings, the eternal one of fierce radiance, having created all the worlds, is worshipped, surrounded by beings in the thousands."}},{"n":13,"text":"नरनारायणौ ब्रह्मा यमः स्थाणुश्च पञ्चमः ।\nउपासते यत्र सत्रं सहस्रयुगपर्यये ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Nara and Narayana, Brahma, Yama and Sthanu, the fifth, take part in a sacrificial session at the turning of a thousand ages."}},{"n":14,"text":"यत्रेष्टं वासुदेवेन सत्रैर्वर्षसहस्रकैः ।\nश्रद्दधानेन सततं शिष्टसंप्रतिपत्तये ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Vasudeva performed sacrifices over thousands of years, always with faith, so that good people might follow his example."}},{"n":15,"text":"सुवर्णमालिनो यूपाश्चित्याश्चाप्यतिभास्वराः ।\nददौ यत्र सहस्राणि प्रयुतानि च केशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The posts were wreathed in gold and the altars shone brilliantly; there Keshava gave away thousands and hundreds of thousands."}},{"n":16,"text":"तत्र गत्वा स जग्राह गदां शङ्खं च भारत ।\nस्फाटिकं च सभाद्रव्यं यदासीद्वृषपर्वणः ।\nकिंकरैः सह रक्षोभिरगृह्णात्सर्वमेव तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going there, Maya took the mace and the conch, Bharata, and the crystal materials for the hall that had belonged to Vrishaparvan; with the help of the Rakshasa servants he took all of it."}},{"n":17,"text":"तदाहृत्य तु तां चक्रे सोऽसुरोऽप्रतिमां सभाम् ।\nविश्रुतां त्रिषु लोकेषु दिव्यां मणिमयीं शुभाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bringing them back, the Asura made a matchless hall, famed in the three worlds, divine, jeweled and beautiful."}},{"n":18,"text":"गदां च भीमसेनाय प्रवरां प्रददौ तदा ।\nदेवदत्तं च पार्थाय ददौ शङ्खमनुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he gave Bhimasena the best of maces, and gave Partha the supreme conch Devadatta."}},{"n":19,"text":"सभा तु सा महाराज शातकुम्भमयद्रुमा ।\nदश किष्कुसहस्राणि समन्तादायताभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hall, great king, with trees of gold, extended ten thousand kishkus in every direction."}},{"n":20,"text":"यथा वह्नेर्यथार्कस्य सोमस्य च यथैव सा ।\nभ्राजमाना तथा दिव्या बभार परमं वपुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shining like fire, like the sun and like the moon, that heavenly hall wore a supremely glorious form."}},{"n":21,"text":"प्रतिघ्नतीव प्रभया प्रभामर्कस्य भास्वराम् ।\nप्रबभौ ज्वलमानेव दिव्या दिव्येन वर्चसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With its radiance it seemed to outshine the sun's blaze; it glowed as if aflame, divine with divine splendor."}},{"n":22,"text":"नगमेघप्रतीकाशा दिवमावृत्य विष्ठिता ।\nआयता विपुला श्लक्ष्णा विपाप्मा विगतक्लमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"It stood covering the sky like a mountain or a cloud, vast, wide and smooth, free of sin and of weariness."}},{"n":23,"text":"उत्तमद्रव्यसंपन्ना मणिप्राकारमालिनी ।\nबहुरत्ना बहुधना सुकृता विश्वकर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was made of the finest materials, encircled by a jeweled wall, rich in gems and wealth, and well made by Vishvakarma."}},{"n":24,"text":"न दाशार्ही सुधर्मा वा ब्रह्मणो वापि तादृशी ।\nआसीद्रूपेण संपन्ना यां चक्रेऽप्रतिमां मयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither the hall of the Dasharhas, nor Sudharma, nor even that of Brahma was so endowed in beauty as the matchless hall Maya made."}},{"n":25,"text":"तां स्म तत्र मयेनोक्ता रक्षन्ति च वहन्ति च ।\nसभामष्टौ सहस्राणि किंकरा नाम राक्षसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Maya had commanded, eight thousand Rakshasas called Kinkaras guarded and carried that hall."}},{"n":26,"text":"अन्तरिक्षचरा घोरा महाकाया महाबलाः ।\nरक्ताक्षाः पिङ्गलाक्षाश्च शुक्तिकर्णाः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They moved in the air, terrible, huge and strong, red-eyed or tawny-eyed, with ears like shells, and fierce strikers."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्यां सभायां नलिनीं चकाराप्रतिमां मयः ।\nवैडूर्यपत्रविततां मणिनालमयाम्बुजाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that hall Maya made a matchless lotus pond, with leaves of lapis lazuli and lotuses with jeweled stalks."}},{"n":28,"text":"पद्मसौगन्धिकवतीं नानाद्विजगणायुताम् ।\nपुष्पितैः पङ्कजैश्चित्रां कूर्ममत्स्यैश्च शोभिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It held lotuses and water lilies, was thronged by many kinds of birds, and was adorned with blossoming lotuses, tortoises and fish."}},{"n":29,"text":"सूपतीर्थामकलुषां सर्वर्तुसलिलां शुभाम् ।\nमारुतेनैव चोद्धूतैर्मुक्ताबिन्दुभिराचिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It had good landing steps, clear water in every season, and was lovely, strewn with pearl-like drops tossed up by the wind."}},{"n":30,"text":"मणिरत्नचितां तां तु केचिदभ्येत्य पार्थिवाः ।\nदृष्ट्वापि नाभ्यजानन्त तेऽज्ञानात्प्रपतन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some kings, coming near that jeweled pool and seeing it, did not recognize it, and in their ignorance fell in."}},{"n":31,"text":"तां सभामभितो नित्यं पुष्पवन्तो महाद्रुमाः ।\nआसन्नानाविधा नीलाः शीतच्छाया मनोरमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All around the hall stood great flowering trees of many kinds, dark, cool-shaded and charming."}},{"n":32,"text":"काननानि सुगन्धीनि पुष्करिण्यश्च सर्वशः ।\nहंसकारण्डवयुताश्चक्रवाकोपशोभिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were fragrant groves and lotus ponds everywhere, with swans and karandava ducks and graced by chakravaka birds."}},{"n":33,"text":"जलजानां च माल्यानां स्थलजानां च सर्वशः ।\nमारुतो गन्धमादाय पाण्डवान्स्म निषेवते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wind, bearing the scent of flowers born in water and on land, waited on the Pandavas."}},{"n":34,"text":"ईदृशीं तां सभां कृत्वा मासैः परिचतुर्दशैः ।\nनिष्ठितां धर्मराजाय मयो राज्ञे न्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made such a hall, Maya completed it in fourteen months and presented it to King Yudhishthira, the king of dharma."}}]}]}